{"id":125738,"imdb":"tt0406551","en":"The Gate of the Sun","orig":"باب الشمس‎‎","ar":null,"tag":null,"ov":"Yousry Nasrallah's powerful adaptation of Lebanese writer Elias Khoury's epic novel of fifty years of Palestinian dispossession, exile, and resistance. The film follows the flight of Younes, his wife Nahila, and those around them, from their village in northern Palestine to a refugee camp in Lebanon. Some vow to continue the struggle, most simply struggle to survive. Unsparingly detailing the impact of the nakba (disaster) on Palestinian life and society and the refugees' often-contentious relationship with their reluctant Lebanese hosts, Gate of the Sun spans generations, mixing personal stories with historical events.","rd":"2004-05-18","rt":278,"g":[10752,10749,18,36],"lang":"ar","budget":0,"revenue":0,"companies":[{"n":"ARTE France Cinéma","logo":"/huC7HqorvUThGIrENrbcHmQVUA0.png","c":"FR"},{"n":"Ognon Pictures","logo":null,"c":"FR"},{"n":"MISR International Films","logo":"/rgUiPgpxE7oKPFgU3GEirqAWEXx.png","c":"EG"}],"countries":["EG","BE","FR","MA","DK"],"langs":["English","Arabic","French"],"col":null,"rel":[{"c":"FR","d":"2004-05-18"}],"dir":["Yousry Nasrallah"],"prod":["Humbert Balsan"],"wri":["Muhammad Suwaid","Yousry Nasrallah","Elias Khoury"],"mus":["Tamer Karawan"],"dop":["Samir Bahzan"],"cast":[{"n":"Hiam Abbass","ch":"Um Youness","p":"/2cz9mO3qhUQeGdVHzWkS2Pwx94l.jpg"},{"n":"Rim Turkhi","ch":"Nahila","p":"/42k9FmE0l9TGgQOta4ogPbmwVlh.jpg"},{"n":"Béatrice Dalle","ch":"Catherine","p":"/3iz1YYnSxgKctHAegL6B7K6AWoD.jpg"},{"n":"Orwa Nyrabia","ch":"Youness","p":null},{"n":"Bassem Samra","ch":"Interrogateur","p":"/tKhneTl9BL6W1jIgTV43o5duFPx.jpg"},{"n":"Darina Al Joundi","ch":"Femme fantôme","p":"/8cbLlrpuUM8gPdL2uM8UNcqFNK7.jpg"},{"n":"Hussein Abou Seada","ch":"Colonel Mehdi","p":null},{"n":"Fadi Abi Samra","ch":"Dr. Amgad","p":"/ttYU20sBXUYimLVFPmfVpjRc4o9.jpg"},{"n":"Ahmad Al Ahmad","ch":"Adnan","p":"/8bhf8NbkWjVhxLIKqfx8BTxB4u9.jpg"},{"n":"Antoine Ba